        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4765_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4765_Lane3" name="Rental Program">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4765_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4765_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4765_Start5" name="Customer disputes a rental charge (W4760), damage/deductible (W4759/W4762)…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4765_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4765_Task6" name="Triage the dispute: rental charge, damage/deductible (W4759/W4762)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Triage the dispute: rental charge, damage/deductible (W4759/W4762), fuel/cleaning/late, LDW, or service; pull the evidence (telematics W4749, photosets W4758/W4759, agreement W4755, billing W4760); attempt first-contact resolution where the evidence supports the customer
Responsible (R): Rental Counter / Rental Program / LP
Accountable (A): Rental Program Manager
Duration: Per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4765_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4765_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4765_Task7" name="For chargebacks (VS-80/card-scheme) or formal complaints (VS-13/W469 DTI)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: For chargebacks (VS-80/card-scheme) or formal complaints (VS-13/W469 DTI): assemble the representment evidence pack (signed agreement + telematics + photoset + billing) and submit within the scheme&#x27;s window (links VS-80 W537/W267 chargeback representment pattern); coordinate with Legal (VS-100) for escalated claims
Responsible (R): Finance / Rental Program / Legal
Accountable (A): Rental Program Manager / Finance
Duration: Per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4765_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4765_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4765_Task8" name="Resolve and close: refund/credit where due, uphold where justified, record the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Resolve and close: refund/credit where due, uphold where justified, record the outcome and root cause; feed repeat issues to process/quality improvement (VS-133) and to analytics (W4768); manage DTI Consumer Act (RA 7394) escalations (W469)
Responsible (R): Rental Program / Finance / Legal
Accountable (A): Rental Program Manager
Duration: Per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4765_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4765_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4765_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4765_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-718 (ensure controlled execution — Incident, Damage, Compliance &amp; Rental Analytics (PA-162.3).) | - CTL-718: disputes resolved with evidence; chargebacks represented within window; DTI escalations handled per W469; outcomes feed improvement
Owner: Rental Program Manager / CX (VS-13)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
